    {
      "name": "Sin Scent (Imprecise) 30 feet",
      "actions": null,
      "traits": [],
      "description": "<p>A sinspawn can smell creatures that reflect its sin as the scent ability. The GM determines which creatures are appropriately sinful.</p>\n<hr />\n<p><details><summary>See rules...</summary>\n<p><p>Scent involves sensing creatures or objects by smell, and is usually a vague sense. The range is listed in the ability, and it functions only if the creature or object being detected emits an aroma (for instance, incorporeal creatures usually do not exude an aroma).</p>\n<p>If a creature emits a heavy aroma or is upwind, the GM can double or even triple the range of scent abilities used to detect that creature, and the GM can reduce the range if a creature is downwind.</p></p></details></p>",
      "collapsed": false
    }
